From 2e121309619669cbfe2b264b199ac01ea46c8e9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:49:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(indoor): straight corridor runs between real junctions
 with right-angle door branches

The shared-corridor compiler now decomposes each checked network into runs
(lanes joined through vertices whose straightest continuation deflects by
less than 30 degrees; short destination spurs and terminal joins do not split
a run) and, longest first, fits each run with one straight centre line, or up
to eight straight pieces, through its cross-section midpoints
(corridor-run-fit.ts). Junctions on the run are projected onto the fit and
every door branch of the run is proposed again against it, preferring a
branch that meets the run within 10 degrees of a right angle; the join slides
along the run. A branch that cannot be proposed again keeps its exact checked
approach and join with one short lane piece to the run.

A run is replaced only if every new run piece, every changed neighbouring
lane piece and every moved door branch passes the same exact support, the
complete network gains no topology contact (identified by the e826098
approach-conflict key and the exact rational contact location, via the new
corridorChainTopologyContacts), and no required original edge's shared-lane
route grows by more than 15 % plus 3 ft. Otherwise that run keeps its checked geometry and the next run is
tried. Loops, islands and genuine corners are kept; original terminals,
endpoints, ownership and access are unchanged; legacy networks are untouched.

- prepareSharedCorridorRouting: if a cell's legacy fallback guides (from
  another network) cross its straight-run guides more than the guides
  compiled without straight runs, the cell is compiled without straight runs
  (report.straightRunsWithdrawn).
- New compiler parameter straightRuns (default on, bound in checkpoints);
  compile-corridor-candidates.ts --without-straight-runs reproduces the
  previous compiler as a separate experiment.
- statistics().straightRuns reports fitted/kept runs by reason, pieces,
  moved junctions, re-proposed, perpendicular and kept door branches.
- Tests: a branched hall with side corridors, a corner, a lobby island loop
  and door recesses (straight hall, perpendicular branches, kept corner,
  both island lanes, support, endpoints, determinism); a door branch that
  cannot be re-proposed; a run whose straight proposal fails support while
  its neighbours are fitted; topology contacts. The join-sliding test
  isolates sliding.
- Regenerate the prepared-display, published-route-runtime and visitor-plan
  runtime bindings, whose module closures include the compiler.

